Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Optionally size the KV cache without memory profiling

With VLLM_SKIP_MEMORY_PROFILING_WITH_KV_CACHE_BYTES=1 and kv_cache_memory_bytes
set, the engine core uses that per-worker KV cache size instead of profiling
the model's peak memory; without the variable nothing changes.

Upstream: vLLM, https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm (Apache License 2.0),
base commit d4004455d2357985830af10e432709b42c820455; the modified file keeps
its SPDX license header. Apply both with `git apply` on that commit.

Provenance: 0001 and 0002, each read from its `diff --git` line on, are the two
file diffs of the uncommitted change in the vLLM checkout the FastAFD alignment
reference was built from; concatenated they are that change as one diff,
sha256 899ee3acce35eee4da5c3ae57e5479782e3faa1173981786f1eafe27e5e303e3.
---
diff --git a/vllm/v1/engine/core.py b/vllm/v1/engine/core.py
index c9503e46d..ae96c6b39 100644
--- a/vllm/v1/engine/core.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/engine/core.py
@@ -247,6 +247,19 @@ class EngineCore:
                 available_gpu_memory = [self.available_gpu_memory_for_kv_cache] * len(
                     kv_cache_specs
                 )
+            elif (
+                os.getenv("VLLM_SKIP_MEMORY_PROFILING_WITH_KV_CACHE_BYTES") == "1"
+                and vllm_config.cache_config.kv_cache_memory_bytes
+            ):
+                available_gpu_memory = [
+                    vllm_config.cache_config.kv_cache_memory_bytes
+                ] * len(kv_cache_specs)
+                self.available_gpu_memory_for_kv_cache = available_gpu_memory[0]
+                logger.warning(
+                    "Skipping model memory profiling and using "
+                    "kv_cache_memory_bytes=%s per worker for KV cache.",
+                    vllm_config.cache_config.kv_cache_memory_bytes,
+                )
             else:
                 # Profiles the peak memory usage of the model to determine how
                 # much memory can be allocated for kv cache.
